  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **One in Seven** (1 review): Reviewer counts this version among their favorites; the organ playing is likened to a heavy locomotive, and the mid-song buildup stands out [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Don't Tell Me**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Comfort**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **One of Those Days**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Mary**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **If This World Were a Song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Callin'**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Waterfall**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Outrage [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2007-08-22.c4.flacf** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 111 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Some audible static in quiet passages, probably from a faulty optical cable, but it barely intrudes on the music [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer saw several shows on this tour and feels the recording captures the band's feel during that distinctive period [2]\n- The trio's older staples are played with notable intensity and bursts of energy, according to the reviewer [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2007-08-22.c4.flacf**: taped by Howie Feltersnatch; transferred by Howie Feltersnatch; source: Studio Projects C4's>PS2>AD20>iRiver H120 [1]. Also: Microphones were DIN, positioned roughly 30 feet back, dead front center [1]",
